/data/
/.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.log
.DS_Store
.claude/
.pytest_cache/

# The frozen tercile cuts are a PRE-REGISTRATION artifact: their entire value is
# that a commit proves they predate the data they are applied to. A frozen file
# that can be deleted and silently refitted is only weakly frozen, so this one
# specific file is tracked. Everything else under /data/ stays ignored.
# The parent directories must be unignored first or the negation cannot match.
!/data/
/data/*
!/data/derived/
/data/derived/*
!/data/derived/regime/
/data/derived/regime/*
!/data/derived/regime/terciles.json
# _manifest.json records row counts, per-column NaN counts, the config and the
# git hash -- what was produced, alongside terciles.json's what was frozen. Same
# provability argument, ~1.7 KB. The parquet outputs (9.8 MB) stay ignored.
!/data/derived/regime/_manifest.json
# The fold schedule is pre-registration-adjacent: §4.2's calendar rule is
# frozen, and a committed folds.json proves the boundaries were not moved
# after results were seen. ~4 KB.
!/data/derived/folds/
/data/derived/folds/*
!/data/derived/folds/folds.json
# grid.json records m*, the eleven multipliers, the derived cap and the A3
# verdict per fold per symbol -- all pre-lift, and the range is not
# extendable afterwards, so a committed copy proves it was not widened.
!/data/derived/sweep/
/data/derived/sweep/*
!/data/derived/sweep/grid.json
# sweep.json is the step 2 deliverable: the per-offset, per-arm, per-population
# aggregates that steps 3 through 8 select from. Steps 3 and 4 are forbidden
# from revisiting step 2, so a committed copy proves which numbers the band
# identification and collapse were performed against. ~200 KB. The per-cell
# JSONL (~7k records) and the trade tables stay ignored -- both are
# reproducible from this hash and are far too large to track.
!/data/derived/sweep/sweep.json
# bands.json is the step 3 deliverable: the K.2 acceptance verdict for every
# grid point, the per-fold bands, the plateau selections and the kill-condition
# verdicts. Step 4 is forbidden from revisiting step 3, so a committed copy
# proves which numbers the collapse was performed against.
!/data/derived/sweep/bands.json
# e6_dispersion.json records the measured sigma, the per-fold trade counts and
# the E6 trigger verdict, against the clean hash the lift was taken at. The
# trigger is pre-committed and cannot be re-decided once sigma is known, so a
# committed copy proves which numbers the fold-architecture decision was made
# on. ~103 KB. The 54 trade tables under trades/ (4.1 MB) stay ignored -- they
# are reproducible from this hash and carry the returns themselves.
!/data/derived/analysis/
/data/derived/analysis/*
!/data/derived/analysis/e6_dispersion.json
# bitget_fees.json is a PROVENANCE artifact: a fee rate nobody can date is a
# rate the admissibility line cannot be defended against. The commit is what
# proves which schedule, retrieved when and from where, report 17's envelope
# was derived from -- and src/costs/envelope.py refuses to run without it, so
# an untracked copy would make the module unrunnable on a fresh clone. ~4 KB,
# no market data in it.
!/data/reference/
/data/reference/*
!/data/reference/bitget_fees.json
# bitget_instruments.json is report 18's provenance artifact: tick size, the
# lot specs it cross-checks against the fee artifact, and ONE point-in-time
# price per symbol used solely to convert a tick into basis points. The price
# is why this must be dated and committed -- the slippage verdict is
# price-conditional, and a commit proves which price it was taken at. It is a
# reference reading, NOT a market data series: no bars, no history, nothing
# from the holdout window. ~2 KB.
!/data/reference/bitget_instruments.json
